# Tracked on purpose. Every EXPO_PUBLIC_ value below is inlined into the
# shipped binary by Babel, so none of it is a secret — it is already readable
# in any installed build. Committing it is what makes it survive build paths
# that only see the committed tree: `eas build` (cloud and --local, because
# eas.json sets requireCommit) and CI both drop the gitignored .env*.local
# files, and a bundle built without these values ships an app that cannot
# reach Supabase at all.
#
# Loaded only when NODE_ENV=production, and .env.production.local / .env.local
# still take priority, so local overrides and `expo start` are unaffected.
# Source of truth stays the EAS `production` environment; refresh with
# `eas env:pull --environment production` and copy any changes here.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://magicbooklet.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://magicbooklet.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_API_BASE_URL=https://magicbooklet.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ildfmhozpibwiopeavfg.supabase.co
